 "equipment_type": "VAV box controller",
 "applies_to": "KMC SimplyVAV controller-actuators for single duct cooling/heating, fan powered with reheat and dual duct VAV boxes.",
 "summary": "SimplyVAV controllers are BACnet MS/TP application specific controllers (B-ASC) with a built-in damper actuator, set up from the STE-8001 wall sensor. The guide lists the objects most likely to be monitored from a BACnet workstation: physical inputs and outputs, setpoint and airflow AVs, status BVs, four multistate values and three PID loops. Objects use short instances and uppercase names (AV5 OCC CL STPT). Not every object exists on every model.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "The guide gives object, name and a short description only: no units (except the two AOs), no read/write column and no state texts. Access here is inferred from what each object is; setpoint and configuration AVs are marked writable.",
  "KMC says this list covers the objects likely to be monitored, not every object, and that changing the configuration of an object can cause unpredictable operation.",
  "Models: BAC-8001 cooling/heating only, BAC-8005 fan and reheat, BAC-8007 dual duct, BAC-8205 fan and reheat with true damper position. Not all objects are present in every model.",
  "Some descriptions are printed as placeholders or repeats (BV 3 'Need For AHU', AV 54 'Analog Value #54', MSV 6 'Multi-state Value #6'); the object names are kept as printed.",
  "Multistate values are printed as MSV1-MSV6 and loops as LOOP1-LOOP3; they are listed here as MV and LO objects."
 ],
